{{DISPLAYTITLE:Help:WantedSort}}

'''Special:WantedSort''' lists [[Help:Wanted pages|wanted pages]] (titles that are linked to but do not exist), with filters and sort options that core [[Special:WantedPages]] does not provide.

This is the detailed user guide. For installation and configuration, see the [https://github.com/Saintapedia/WantedSort extension README] or ask a site administrator.

== Opening the report ==

Go to '''[[Special:WantedSort]]'''.

You can also bookmark a filtered view:

* By subpage (namespace name or ID): <code>Special:WantedSort/Category</code> or <code>Special:WantedSort/14</code>
* By query string: <code>Special:WantedSort?namespace=14&sort=links&dir=desc&limit=50</code>

== Filter form ==

{| class="wikitable"
! Field !! Purpose
|-
| '''Namespace''' || Limit results to one namespace, or show all.
|-
| '''Sort by''' || Link count, title, or namespace.
|-
| '''Direction''' || Ascending or descending.
|-
| '''Results per page''' || Page size (20–500; fewer options if the wiki has “miser mode” enabled).
|}

Click '''Filter''' to apply. Column headers in the results table re-sort and reset to the first page.

=== How namespace is chosen when you first open the page ===

# Explicit <code>?namespace=</code> in the URL (empty value means all namespaces)
# Subpage path (<code>Special:WantedSort/…</code>)
# Site default set by administrators (<code>$wgWantedSortDefaultNamespace</code>), if any
# Otherwise: all namespaces

== Reading the results ==

{| class="wikitable"
! Column !! Meaning
|-
| '''Page title''' || Missing title (red link). Creating the page will remove it from this list once links are re-evaluated.
|-
| '''Namespace''' || Namespace of the missing title.
|-
| '''Incoming links''' || How many pages link to this missing title (above the wiki’s threshold).
|-
| '''What links here''' || Jump to [[Special:WhatLinksHere]] for that title.
|}

Use '''previous''' / '''next''' for pagination. The status line shows the range of rows on the current page (not a total count of all wanted pages).

=== Notices you may see ===

* '''Miser mode''' — The wiki limits expensive queries. Caps are lower; results may be slightly stale.
* '''Cached results''' — This page of results came from cache and may not reflect the very latest links.

== Export to CSV ==

'''You must be logged in''' to export.

# Apply the filters you want (export uses those filters, not only the current page of the table).
# Click '''Export to CSV''', or open the same filters with <code>&export=csv</code> in the URL.

{| class="wikitable"
! CSV column !! Content
|-
| <code>title</code> || Prefixed title
|-
| <code>namespace</code> || Namespace label
|-
| <code>namespace_id</code> || Numeric namespace ID
|-
| <code>links</code> || Incoming link count
|}

'''Limits:''' Up to 5,000 rows normally, or 1,000 if miser mode is on. If the list is longer, the file ends with a <code># Export truncated…</code> comment.

'''Security:''' Titles that start with <code>=</code>, <code>+</code>, <code>-</code>, or <code>@</code> are prefixed so spreadsheet programs do not treat them as formulas.

Anonymous users see a log-in prompt instead of the download link.

== Tips for cleaning up wanted pages ==

* Start with the highest link counts (default sort) — fixing those helps the most readers.
* Filter to one namespace (e.g. main or Category) to work in batches.
* Use '''What links here''' to decide whether to create the article, fix a typo, or retarget links.
* After creating many pages, wait for caches (or ask an admin) if the list looks stale.

